From 95e4e2660b1b78aad80517aeddc7509809d04fc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:03:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] omp: enable remote compaction when the provider compacts
 natively
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

omp 18.15 asks a provider for its own compaction (POST
{baseUrl}/responses with a compaction_trigger) only with
remoteCompaction enabled on the provider, and on the loopback gateway
with v2StreamingEnabled too. magpie never wrote the block, so a trigger
of omp's was answered magpie's summary ("magpie1:"), which omp's V2
check takes for a successful seal — it never falls back to its own
summarization, and the conversation goes on from magpie's summary
unasked.

magpie now writes remoteCompaction: {enabled: true,
v2StreamingEnabled: true} under its provider in models.yml when every
model the write lists as openai-responses — a routing group by its
every member — compacts natively (provider.CompactsOn: the provider's
Compaction row on, its wire carrying the trigger, the model asked on
Responses there). That is asked of the write's own list, not of the
catalog at sync time, as nativeCompactionFor also needs a key the
request would go over now (plannedCarrier). No model listed as
openai-responses, none written: with it omp would send triggers
codexCompact answers "magpie1:" to, the global switch #1099 rejected.
A block the user wrote stays as it is, enabled: false included (#2030's
keeping of what omp's schema doesn't name).

When omp's trigger can't be carried, the answer is an error, never
codexCompact's item: V2 installs that and does not fall back. Codex
keeps the summary path, which it does fall back from. Not done:
remoteCompaction.api (it would send the models asked on other APIs down
the Responses compact path), omp's default protocol (#4982), and POST
/v1/responses/compact.

Fixes #5065
The fix follows the reporter's spec: wwwhynot3 read omp 18.15's
binaries and defined the write rule, the error and the exclusions
exactly.

